  "title": "indigo_agent_scheduler: SCHEDULER.md, the first VISIBILITY minute counts from the end of the running run or hook",
  "description": "indigo_drivers/agent_scheduler/doc/SCHEDULER.md (VISIBILITY Algorithm step 1, line 719) says the first minute is the earliest whole minute 'from now on' at which a task can start. vis_first_start() counts from the planning state's time, which is the end of the running task run or hook when one is running, otherwise now (review note of fd0dfe3b). Correct the wording; documentation only, no code change.",
